window.GLOSS={};
window.EN={"1":"Through an unforeseen turn of events, Sigurd, branded a traitor by the very homeland he loved,","2":"fled in despair to the independent northern nation of Silesse.","3":"The kingdom of Silesse, founded by the Wind Crusader Sety,","4":"had been protected by its valiant Pegasus Knights and wind mages, and for the hundred years since its founding,","5":"had never been invaded by another nation, maintaining complete neutrality.","6":"But when the king died a few years ago, conflict arose within the royal family over the succession,","7":"and even this once-peaceful nation now showed sudden signs of war.","8":"The late king had a son, Prince Levin, by Queen Lahna,","9":"but the ambitious younger brother, Duke Dakar, objecting to Levin's succession to the throne,","10":"entrenched himself in Saxony Castle, and as if in answer to that,","11":"the youngest brother, Duke Maios, also began gathering troops at Tove Castle.","12":"In the midst of this situation, Prince Levin had no choice but to leave the country,","13":"but the royal family's ambitions knew no bounds, and Silesse's beautiful land","14":"was now on the verge of being consumed by the flames of war.","15":"Lord Sigurd, Lady Lahna has come to see you.","16":"Lady Lahna has?","17":"Lord Sigurd, how is life at Seiren Castle? Have you grown used to it yet?","18":"Yes, thank you. I'm truly grateful for Lady Lahna's kindness.","19":"In such a small castle, you must be inconvenienced in various ways, but please bear with it a little longer.","20":"I've written letters many times, stating that you are innocent, and sent them off,","21":"but there's still no reply from King Azmur.","22":"That's... probably because Chancellor Reptor is intercepting them. The one who framed my father was likely him too...","23":"Lord Sigurd... I understand how you feel, but you mustn't be impatient.","24":"And you mustn't resent people either. Nothing good comes from hatred. I'll surely find a way.","25":"Please wait just a little longer.","26":"Thank you. I really don't know how to thank you enough, Lady Lahna...","27":"Please don't worry about that. Oh, and that reminds me, Lord Sigurd,","28":"I hear there was happy news in Grannvale.","29":"Happy news?","30":"Yes, it seems the late Prince Kurth had a daughter. The whole country's abuzz over her discovery.","31":"What!? Is that really true!?","32":"King Azmur met her himself, and apparently knew at a single glance.","33":"Of course, there's also the mark of Naga—there's no mistaking she's a direct descendant of the royal house of Belhalla.","34":"I see... that's wonderful. So the royal bloodline won't die out after all.","35":"And you know, apparently the princess is in love with Lord Arvis.","36":"The king has approved, and they're said to be holding a grand wedding ceremony soon.","37":"With Lord Arvis?","38":"From what those who've seen her say, she's a very beautiful princess, and she and Lord Arvis make a wonderful couple,","39":"and I hear both of them looked very happy.","40":"Heh heh, young people these days. Lord Sigurd, you too... oh... I'm sorry... your own wife...","41":"My wife... Deirdre is still missing...","42":"It's been over a year now, and Celice has grown up so much, but I still haven't been able to find her.","43":"Lord Sigurd, please don't lose heart. I'm sure she'll be found, so...","44":"Yes, I believe that too. I have this feeling that I'll surely be reunited with Deirdre someday.","45":"Lady Lahna, it'll be nightfall soon. We should be heading back.","46":"Oh, that's right, it's already this late. Lord Sigurd, just one last word.","47":"Please be careful of Duke Maios at Tove Castle. He's wanted this castle for a long time.","48":"So he might attack at any moment. If it comes to a battle, we really should support you, but...","49":"Silesse is being targeted by Duke Dakar of Saxony. You mustn't let your defenses down.","50":"Sending troops to help us is exactly what Duke Dakar would want.","51":"Please don't worry about us. I'll crush the Tove army with just my own men, you'll see.","52":"I see. You and your men are seasoned warriors, aren't you.","53":"Ah, I've been talking far too long. Well then, Lord Sigurd, please take care.","54":"Lady Lahna, it's you who should take care.","55":"Good, preparations are complete. As planned, attack Seiren Castle.","56":"Show those traitors the terror of us wind-users!","57":"What? Maios of Tove has finally moved his troops!","58":"Fufufu... this is getting interesting. Isn't it so, Pamela?","59":"Indeed. Lord Sigurd's army may be a gathering of deserters, but they possess formidable strength.","60":"If Duke Maios can draw them in, our conquest of Silesse should be easy.","61":"Mm, we already have a secret pact with Grannvale as well.","62":"Prince Andrei's reinforcements should arrive before long too.","63":"Fufufu... Pamela, the day I become King of Silesse isn't far off now.","64":"As you say...","65":"[Only if Edain and Azel are a couple]","66":"Azel, take care of yourself.","67":"Yeah, you too, Edain.","68":"But, somehow it's strange... I never imagined things would turn out like this with you.","69":"Is it because I'm younger than you?","70":"No, that's not it, but...","71":"Even I can't believe it myself.","72":"That Edain became my wife—it feels like I'm dreaming somehow.","73":"Huh, why? Is it strange, you and me?","74":"You were too dazzling for me...","75":"The first time I saw you, I was still a kid, but my heart pounded and wouldn't stop.","76":"From that day on, I kept thinking only of you...","77":"Heh heh, oh, Azel.","78":"I feel kind of embarrassed... oh, that's right, here, take this.","79":"This is called the Rescue Staff—it can call someone far away back to your side.","80":"I think you'd be able to use it.","81":"Azel, I'm happy. You're the kindest person, anyone, to me... you're my treasure...","82":"[Only if Edain and Mideel are a couple]","83":"Mideel, take this bow with you.","84":"Isn't this the Hero's Bow? Is it really all right for me to have it?","85":"Yes, I bought it for you. The Pegasus Knights of Silesse are a terrifying enemy.","86":"With this bow, I'm sure it'll protect you.","87":"Lady Edain, I feel as if I'm still dreaming.","88":"Because I've dreamed of this happening for so long.","89":"I've been dreaming the same dream too. To tell the truth I was lonely—I was waiting for you all this time...","90":"Mideel, come back safe no matter what, and then, call me Edain, I'm praying for you.","91":"[Only if Edain and Jamka are a couple]","92":"Jamka, please use this bow.","93":"This is the Hero's Bow, isn't it. Is it really all right for me to have it?","94":"I want you to have it with you.","95":"The Pegasus Knights of Silesse are a terrifying enemy, but this bow should protect you.","96":"Thank you, Edain. I'll treasure this bow, thinking of it as you. Once the fighting's over, let's meet slowly.","97":"Jamka...... I'm praying for your safety.","98":"Father Claude, I'm sorry, dragging even you into this.","99":"No, it is I who feel sorry for not being able to help you.","100":"I intended to return to Grannvale and tell His Majesty the truth,","101":"but Reptor and his men beat me to it. Now I too am one of the traitors.","102":"I can no longer bear Reptor and his men's way of doing things.","103":"At this point, I intend to go to Grannvale even by force, and clear my name.","104":"No, war is not a good thing. It's the powerless commoners who suffer. Lord Sigurd, you must be patient.","105":"But, Father Claude!","106":"I understand how you feel, but the door of destiny has already been opened.","107":"There's nothing more we can do about it with our own strength now.","108":"[Only if neither Tiltyu nor Azel has a sweetheart]","109":"Azel, wait up.","110":"Tiltyu, is it. What's wrong?","111":"There's something I'd like you to listen to.","112":"Huh? To me?","113":"Yeah, is that all right? We've known each other since we were little, after all.","114":"There's no one else I can talk about things like this with.","115":"Sounds kind of serious. All right, if it's something I can help with, tell me.","116":"Yeah... you see, I,","117":"I came along with Father Claude without thinking about anything, but I wonder if that was really the right thing to do...","118":"Why would you think something like that?","119":"Because everyone's being considerate toward me, that's why.","120":"In front of me, nobody talks about Father...","121":"I see... that's why you're lonely. But, you know, everyone likes you.","122":"It's just that they're troubled because they don't know how to treat you, I think.","123":"Well, you'll get used to it eventually. Don't worry.","124":"Yeah... you're right... thank you, Azel, I somehow feel cheered up.","125":"Hahaha, Tiltyu's energy is second to none.","126":"Whenever you're lonely, I'll always be there for you, so just say so without holding back.","127":"Yeah... thanks.","128":"[Only if Silvia, Fury, and Levin all have no sweetheart]","129":"Hey, Fury, could it be... do you like Levin?","130":"What!? ...I'm... that's not... it's just that Prince Levin is important to Silesse, so...","131":"Oh, I see, so it's fine for me and Levin to go out, then?","132":"Wh-why, I don't particularly mind...","133":"Really~? You're not forcing yourself, are you?","134":"I-I'm not forcing myself at all. Why would I have to force myself?","135":"Suuure~, well, if that's the case, I'll just take him for myself, Levin, I mean...","136":"Ah... but you know, someone who's to become the queen of Silesse should have Lady Lahna's kind of elegance...","137":"Are you saying I'm no good!? That's so rude!","138":"Eh... that's not...","139":"Hmph, fine! I won't lose, you know!","140":"...............","141":"Magic has its strengths and weaknesses too, same as weapons. Fire is strong against wind, wind against lightning, lightning against fire.","142":"But light and dark have the advantage over all of them. Think carefully as you fight.","143":"The blood of the gods carries all sorts of power.","144":"It lets you use higher-level items, and your abilities as a warrior improve faster too.","145":"Of course, only a limited few still carry on that bloodline, though.","146":"Only direct descendants can fully inherit the power of the gods.","147":"That's why only direct descendants can use the god-given items known as holy relics.","148":"But, if blood from the same bloodline were to mix, the blood would thicken, and one could even gain the power of the gods.","149":"But that, you see, is forbidden as a taboo thing...","150":"The power of the Silesse royal family is wind, bestowed by the wind god Forseti.","151":"The power of House Vertomer is fire, bestowed by the fire god Fala.","152":"The power of House Freege is lightning, bestowed by the thunder god Thor.","153":"The power of the dark god Loptous is darkness—the only thing that can oppose it is the holy power of the holy god Naga.","154":"And the only ones who carry on Naga's power are Grannvale's royal house of Heim.","155":"[If visited with Silvia]","156":"Oh! Lord Sigurd's army has come to help us! Hm? You're a dancer?","157":"If you don't mind, won't you dance for us, please,","158":"in times like these there's nothing fun to enjoy every day.","159":"Sure, I don't mind! If my dancing can cheer you all up, I'll dance as much as you like!","160":"...All right, here I go!!","161":"There!","162":"Hyah!","163":"Yah!","164":"Phew~, how was it? Did it cheer you up a little?","165":"Ohh! What a wonderful dance! Somehow I feel like giving it one more try now!","166":"Thank you. It's not much of a thank-you, but let me give you this magic sword. I'm sure it'll protect you.","167":"[If visited with any other unit]","168":"It's said that those of direct crusader descent develop a holy mark somewhere on their body during childhood.","169":"Prince Kurth's princess too, by a mark on her forehead,","170":"was confirmed to be a direct descendant of the saint Heim, they say.","171":"If Prince Kurth's princess has a child, that child will be the heir to the Grannvale royal house.","172":"Lord Arvis's power, as the one who'll become the princess's husband, will only grow greater.","173":"[If the drawbridge hasn't been raised yet]","174":"The bridge over the Tove river is a drawbridge managed by the lord, Lord Maios.","175":"If it's raised, you can't cross without the key.","176":"But, a skilled person, like a thief, might be able to pick the lock.","177":"[If the drawbridge has already been raised]","178":"The bridge over the Tove river is a drawbridge managed by the lord, Lord Maios.","179":"If it's raised, you can't cross without the key.","180":"But, a skilled person, like a thief, might be able to pick the lock.","181":"...What, the bridge is already down? How did you know that?","182":"Ugh... this shouldn't be happening...","183":"Dietvar, I leave the rest to you...","184":"[If fought against Fury]","185":"Fufufu, Fury, is it. What good timing to run into you here.","186":"I'll take that head of yours as a gift for Lord Maios.","187":"That won't happen, Dietvar. I'm not the Fury from back then anymore. I won't lose to you either!","188":"Heh, that crybaby Fury, talking big! Don't make me laugh!!","189":"[If fought against any other unit]","190":"I am Dietvar, one of the Four Pegasus Knights of Silesse.","191":"I feel for you, but you'll have to die!","192":"Ugh... of all people, me...","193":"What, the traitors from Seiren are closing in on Tove here!? Hey, go raise the drawbridge at the Tove river!","194":"Fufufu, without this key, they can't cross the bridge. I can just picture their shocked faces now.","195":"What, I've got this key... let's see... there.","196":"[If fought against Levin]","197":"Keh, I wondered who it was—Lahna's foolish son. You, you've come back, have you.","198":"Sorry, Uncle, but you'll have to die. It's also for the sake of protecting Silesse.","199":"[If fought against any other unit]","200":"Traitors! I'll hand that head of yours over to Grannvale!","201":"Ugh... that can't be...","202":"Lord Sigurd, the town's elder says he'd like to meet you.","203":"I see, I wanted to meet him too. Bring him in here.","204":"Lord Sigurd, thank you for bringing down Lord Maios.","205":"The townspeople are all pleased too.","206":"What? Why? I thought I was resented as an invader.","207":"Lord Maios was no lord at all—just a tyrant.","208":"Not a single one of us people of Silesse fails to adore Lady Lahna.","209":"I see, that's how it was... then, elder, I leave this town in your hands.","210":"I imagine Lady Lahna will give instructions eventually,","211":"but until then, please protect this town yourselves.","212":"Understood...","213":"Lord Sigurd, Lady Lahna is Silesse's treasure, one who loves peace. Please protect her with your strength.","214":"Yes, I understand well. With all my strength, I promise to protect Queen Lahna!","215":"So Tove has fallen... heh, my foolish brother. Not knowing he'd become my sacrificial pawn, what a pitiful fellow.","216":"Good, Pamela, now's our chance. Lead the Pegasus Knights and sortie.","217":"Capture Silesse Castle before Sigurd can rush over as reinforcements.","218":"Yes sir, leave it to me!","219":"Lady Lahna, Pamela's unit has left Saxony. They're headed for this castle!","220":"What!? Is that true!? Duke Dakar has finally shown his true colors, hasn't he.","221":"Please rest easy. My unit will hold off Pamela's unit.","222":"Mahnya, will you be all right? I hear Pamela is a fearsome Pegasus Knight.","223":"Yes, she certainly possesses formidable strength.","224":"But I too am one of the Four Pegasus Knights of Silesse. I will never fight a shameful battle.","225":"I'm sorry, Mahnya, knowing your feelings as I do... I...","226":"This is simply the only way of life I know how to live... Lady Lahna, please don't worry about it.","227":"Well then, I'll be off now. Mahnya's unit, sortie!","228":"Oh, it's Lord Andrei! You've finally come.","229":"Ho, truly magnificent as ever... as expected of Jungby's archer-knight corps.","230":"Fufufu... my House Jungby has lost its father too, and my sister has sided with the rebels.","231":"Now it is I who lead the archer-knight corps as head of House Jungby.","232":"As long as I have this Vaegrite, there's nothing to fear from Pegasus Knights. Well, just watch and be at ease.","233":"[If fought against Levin]","234":"Why, Prince Levin, it's been a while.","235":"I've already finished off Mahnya for you, ho ho ho...","236":"Damn you, Pamela!! You, of all people...","237":"Heh, this is all because of you, Lord Levin, isn't it...","238":"[If fought against Fury]","239":"Oh my, it's Fury. So you came back after all.","240":"Pamela!! How dare you hurt my big sister... I won't forgive you!","241":"Hmph, don't get cocky, you little chick!","242":"I'll send you off to join Mahnya too. Prepare yourself!!","243":"[If fought against any other unit]","244":"Heh, small fries, die!","245":"I-impossible...","246":"I'm sorry, you all have done nothing wrong, but...","247":"Ah, Fury...... Lord Levin...","248":"Guhahaha, they fall so entertainingly.","249":"Just like catching dragonflies, isn't it.","250":"Pamela, it's been a while. We trained together as knights once, you and I,","251":"but I never imagined it would come to this, that we'd fight each other.","252":"Mahnya, is it... you fool, forever swearing loyalty to a queen you know is doomed to fall.","253":"I'll be the one to defeat you and take the top spot among the Four Pegasus Knights of Silesse. Don't take it personally.","254":"It's you who's the fool. But, well, if this is fate, it can't be helped.","255":"Understood. Let's fight a battle we need not be ashamed of, as fellow knights of Silesse.","256":"Heh, soft as ever...","257":"What, Mahnya's died in battle!? Ahh, how could this be... Mahnya, I'm sorry, forgive me...","258":"Silesse has fallen, has it. That's the end of our duty then. Let's return home to Grannvale!","259":"Fufufu... Silesse Castle has finally fallen into my hands.","260":"Good, send the wind-users south of the Silesse river to firm up the defenses.","261":"And Donovan, you lead the axe fighters and occupy Silesse.","262":"But don't kill Queen Lahna. That woman's an important hostage.","263":"Right, leave it to me.","264":"Hurry, all of you, you must flee!","265":"But, what about Lady Lahna...","266":"Never mind about me! Now, hurry!!","267":"Everyone! Let's do as Lady Lahna says! Come on, run!","268":"What, the citizens of Silesse have run off!","269":"Damn it, those bastards, making fools of us—you lot, I don't care, go kill every last one of them.","270":"Don't let even one of them escape.","271":"Please wait! Those people are mere civilians.","272":"I don't care what happens to me, but please, spare them at least.","273":"That won't do. I'll teach you well what happens if you defy Lord Dakar.","274":"Ahh...","275":"Fufufu... that Donovan, he's doing quite well.","276":"What a hopeless scoundrel. Watching the way you people operate makes me sick.","277":"You're one to talk—a gang of murderers who'll kill anyone indiscriminately for money.","278":"They weren't wrong to call you Reimia of Hell.","279":"Ho ho ho, well, thanks for the compliment. By the way, what's the job this time?","280":"For now, just defend this castle. Sigurd's men might come attacking.","281":"What, that's all? Aah, how boring.","282":"Hey, everyone, this time it's a mop-up job on routed soldiers. Just hang around the castle as you like!","283":"What, the army from Seiren is headed for this castle? Damn it, those traitors!!","284":"You lot, quit dawdling and get to defending the castle! Don't let them get close!","285":"Hello, Father.","286":"Oh, and you are?","287":"It's me, Silvia!","288":"Miss Silvia? But what happened to you? Were you attacked by bandits or something?","289":"Why do you ask?","290":"Well, it's hard to say, but... you're only in your underwear...","291":"Huh, oh no, Father, don't tell me you've never seen a dancer before?","292":"This is my costume. It's like your robe, Father.","293":"I see, I see... but aren't you cold?","294":"Nope, if anything I'm hot. My heart's burning up.","295":"Is dancing really that much fun?","296":"Yeah! I love to dance!!","297":"I see... what about your parents?","298":"I'm an orphan. When I was little, a guild master picked me up and trained me in dance.","299":"But, that guy was a terrible man—he'd whip me if anything happened.","300":"I finally got sick of it and ran away a year ago.","301":"I see... that's an awful story.","302":"My own little sister, if she were alive, would be about your age, so I can't help but take it to heart.","303":"Father has a little sister?","304":"Yes, she was taken away when she was still a baby.","305":"I kept searching the whole time, but I still haven't found her...","306":"Hmm... if Father's little sister is a princess or something, I bet she's elegant and beautiful, not like me...","307":"No, you are a beautiful person. And you have elegance too. I can tell, you know.","308":"Huh... really... Father...","309":"Yes, I never tell lies.","310":"I'm happy... no one's ever told me something like that before... it feels strange somehow...","311":"Huh, I'm even crying... what's wrong with me...","312":"Oh, you saved me, thank you.","313":"Ahh, you're going to save me, aren't you. Thank you so much.","314":"Heh heh heh... die!","315":"Ugh... you lot, you're too strong...","316":"[If Dakar has not been defeated]","317":"Lady Lahna, are you safe!? I'm sorry the reinforcements were late.","318":"No, Lord Sigurd, thank you so much for coming.","319":"Because I'm so unreliable, so many lives were lost—it pains me endlessly.","320":"Mahnya especially, it's hard for me...","321":"Lady Lahna, please don't lose heart. I will avenge Lady Mahnya.","322":"As for myself, I cannot find it in me to forgive Duke Dakar either.","323":"Please allow me to march on Saxony.","324":"Duke Dakar subjected innocent civilians to such terrible treatment. He's nothing but a murderer.","325":"I think it's only right that he receive punishment.","326":"Understood. I'll head for the conquest of Saxony now. Please wait with a peaceful heart.","327":"It's you who should take care, Lord Sigurd. Don't push yourself too hard. Once the conquest of Saxony ends safely, let's meet again then.","328":"[If Dakar has already been defeated]","329":"Lady Lahna, are you safe!? I'm sorry the reinforcements were late.","330":"No, Lord Sigurd, thank you so much for coming.","331":"Because I'm so unreliable, so many lives were lost—it pains me endlessly.","332":"Mahnya especially, it's hard for me...","333":"Lady Lahna, please don't lose heart. I have avenged Lady Mahnya.","334":"I apologize for advancing troops on my own without your permission.","335":"Don't worry about that at all. I'm truly grateful to you, Lord Sigurd.","336":"I'll come to Saxony Castle later myself. Let's meet again then.","337":"[Only if Dakar has not been defeated]","338":"What, Silesse has been retaken by the traitors from Seiren!?","339":"Donovan, just what on earth was he doing...","340":"[Only if Reimia has not been defeated] Damn it, it can't be helped. Order Reimia to sortie. Don't let them get close to this castle!","341":"[Only if Pamela has not been defeated] Tell Pamela's unit to pursue Sigurd's army too. If it's come to this, there's nothing left but all-out war!","342":"[Only if neither Dakar nor Reimia has been defeated]","343":"That Dakar, what's he panicking about. Everyone, let's go, it's a perfect little warm-up job.","344":"Sigurd, sorry for the trouble.","345":"Levin, is it. Sorry about Mahnya.","346":"I never imagined Jungby's archer-knight corps would be here.","347":"No, I'm the one at fault... I was too soft.","348":"I should have helped my mother and protected the country, but instead I ran away,","349":"and Mahnya ended up dying as if taking my place...","350":"You'd better not blame yourself like that. To make sure Mahnya's death wasn't in vain, cherish Lady Lahna.","351":"Yeah, I know that much, at least.","352":"Then that's fine... oh, and Levin,","353":"you have gone to see Lady Lahna already, haven't you. Don't forget, it's important.","354":"[Only if neither Fury nor Levin has a sweetheart]","355":"Lord Levin...","356":"...Fury... I'm sorry, please forgive me...","357":"Lord Levin has feelings for Lady Mahnya...","358":"Ahh......","359":"Just as I thought... I'm sorry, I didn't know anything...","360":"Fury, that's not it. It's true that when I was young I admired Mahnya.","361":"But now it's different, now it's you...","362":"What!? ...","363":"I like you...","364":"Mother, are you safe? I heard Silesse had fallen and I was worried.","365":"Levin, thank you for coming. It seems you've finally become an adult who can keep a promise.","366":"I suppose that's thanks to Lord Sigurd too.","367":"Oh come on, Mother, that makes it sound like I'm a child.","368":"Lord Sigurd and I aren't even that far apart in age...","369":"The difference between you and Lord Sigurd is as great as that between an adult and a child.","370":"You too should hurry and become as fine as he is, and put my mind at ease.","371":"Mahnya's gone now too, after all...","372":"...Mahnya died as if in my place. This time, at least, I've learned my lesson.","373":"Mother, from now on, I will protect you in Mahnya's place.","374":"I will never again let myself be far from your side.","375":"Levin... to think you'd say something so kind...","376":"But, just hearing those words is enough. From now on, you should keep helping Lord Sigurd.","377":"He needs your strength.","378":"But then, Mother, what about you...","379":"It's all right, Levin.","380":"As a descendant of the Wind Crusader, you must watch over this world and guide it in the right direction.","381":"Now is the time, I think, to entrust you with the holy wind tome, Forseti.","382":"Now, Levin, receive it.","383":"This is... Forseti, passed down in our royal family... ahh, this power... this warmth...","384":"Levin, never forget—the Wind Crusader flows gently, like the wind,","385":"and guides the world toward warmth. Fighting is never one's mission.","386":"Yes, I understand. That's exactly the way of life I want most.","387":"That's right, surely you truly are a child of the wind.","388":"Levin... now go. Take care of yourself... don't be reckless...","389":"Mother...","390":"Hurry and go! ...Please, I beg you...","391":"Yes... well then, Mother, please take care too.","392":"Ahh...... Levin......","393":"Fufufu... you lot are such fools.","394":"I-impossible...","395":"[If fought against Levin]","396":"Ugh... Levin... you...","397":"Dakar! How dare you, Mahnya! I won't let even you off easy!","398":"What insolence! Die, Levin!","399":"[If fought against any other unit]","400":"The throne of Silesse suits only me! I won't let the likes of you get in my way!","401":"Ugh... even my ambition, it ends here...","402":"Lord Sigurd, Lady Lahna has come.","403":"Lord Sigurd, that was a fierce battle. Are you unhurt?","404":"Yes, somehow I'm safe.","405":"Lord Sigurd, if possible, could you stay garrisoned at this Saxony Castle as it is?","406":"Duke Langobalt of Grannvale has subdued Lubeck Castle to the east of Saxony with a great army.","407":"The people of Silesse are worried it might turn into a war with Grannvale.","408":"Lady Lahna, Langobalt's corps has come on campaign in order to subjugate us.","409":"I don't want to drag the people of Silesse, who have cared for me, into the flames of war.","410":"I intend to sortie from this castle at once and settle things with Langobalt.","411":"That's reckless. I can't imagine you winning.","412":"If we don't go to them, they'll just come attacking us. Lady Lahna, there's no more time.","413":"I see, how sad...","414":"Lady Lahna, this past year, you've felt to me like my own real mother, and they truly were peaceful days for my heart.","415":"I lost my mother when I was young, and grew up without knowing a mother's love,","416":"but here in Silesse, I feel like I've come to know that warmth for the first time.","417":"Lady Lahna, please take care, and I pray from my heart that we may meet again someday.","418":"That goes for me too, Lord Sigurd. Please stay safe, and don't push yourself too hard.","419":"I pray with all my heart that you may be reunited with Lady Deirdre."};
